# Fixture: podnews-transcript. A real publisher episode (Podnews Daily,
# 2026-09-25) whose feed advertises a text/vtt transcript. Needs the network:
# the save fetches the transcript from podnews.net and playback streams the
# enclosure through the publisher's op3.dev prefix. Widths come from the driver.
settle 30
assert snap item-count >= 1
assert snap item-id == podnews-260925
act pane:notes
settle 10
# Nothing is saved yet: the pane offers the advertised transcript and no cues.
assert snap transcript-cues == 0
capture transcript-offer

# The listener saves it explicitly, through the shipping button, not a lane
# verb. The lane cannot see the fetch thread, so this is a frame budget, not a
# wait; the file is 7 KiB and the bound generous.
# Logical-space click at the button's centre (960x640 artboard): the probe's
# own selector layout resolved role:button to a point the host did not route
# to this button (2026-09-26), so this receipt is pinned to one artboard.
pointer-click 520 221
settle 240
assert snap transcript-item == podnews-260925
assert snap transcript-cues >= 80
capture transcript-saved

# The episode must actually play from the publisher, from the start. Frame
# budgets while playing are small on purpose: with 90 cue rows mounted a
# playing frame took ~1.25 s in the debug build (2026-09-26 pacing run), so
# eight frames is ten seconds of wall clock, not a blink.
act seek:0
act play
settle 8
assert event transport PLAYING
act pause
settle 20

# An external seek lands inside a cue interval (0:12.020 -> 0:16.800) and the
# list must mark it without a click on the list.
act seek:12500
settle 30
assert snap transcript-active >= 1
capture transcript-active

# A cue click issues the shipping seek: the 0:06.600 row (logical y 353 sits
# inside it whether or not the notice bar is showing) moves the playhead there
# and becomes the active row.
pointer-click 600 353
settle 20
assert snap position-ms >= 6000
assert snap position-ms <= 9800
assert snap transcript-active >= 1
capture transcript-cue-seek
log transcript_live complete
